OL,3,GNEWSAThe footballer who was the world's
OL,4,Afirst cross-border signing             
OL,6,FIt might seen unthinkable in today's   
OL,7,Fera of huge wages and multi-million    
OL,8,Fpound transfer fees, but the early days
OL,9,Fof football were strictly an amateur   
OL,10,Faffair.                                
OL,12,FThere was fierce debate throughout the 
OL,13,F1870s and 1880s regarding payment of   
OL,14,Fplayers, as clubs increasingly sought  
OL,15,Fto secure the best talent.             
OL,17,FAt the forefront of this were a number 
OL,18,Fof Scots. Among them was James 'Jimmy' 
OL,19,FLang, a former shipyard worker         
OL,20,Fconsidered by some historians to be the
OL,21,Fworld's first migrant professional     
OL,22,Ffootball player.                       
OL,23,APub: 20-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
